{
  "suite": "chip_auth",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "Chip Authentication dispatch + key material. Pins the eight CA suites' keyAgreement/cipher/keyLength/protocolOIDString tables and their InvalidDataPassed rejections, the two CA-public-key OID names, the SubjectPublicKeyInfo parser that replaces upstream's d2i_PUBKEY (named-curve, explicit prime-field ECParameters, X9.42 dhpublicnumber and PKCS#3 dhKeyAgreement, plus the nil-contract rejects), the CA session-key derivation composed from the OID (cipherAlg + keyLength into the KDF, ENC then MAC), and the infer-OID fallback for pubkey-only DG14s. SPKI fixtures marked openssl-generated are `openssl genpkey`/`openssl pkey -pubout` output, an oracle independent of both runners; `publicKey` is upstream's getPublicKeyData (EC_POINT_point2oct uncompressed / BN_bn2bin) and `domain` the EC_GROUP or DH parameters, both derivable on either side. Upstream's DH keySeed shape (stripped secret left-aligned in a DH_size(p) zero buffer) travels as a literal keySeed here; the composition itself is exercised end-to-end by ca_session_dh_aes_chaining.",
  "runners": [
    "dart",
    "swift"
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "chipAuthInfo.oidInfo id-CA-DH-3DES-CBC-CBC",
